{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc. Take you, etc. a man in whom is ruach.</b> One needs to know why it says <b>take for yourself</b>; further, why it says <b>a man in whom is ruach</b> — is there any person who does not have ruach? Further, one needs to know what this juxtaposition is. However, according to what I explained in the words of Moses, the answer arrives: the meaning of saying ״take for yourself״ is — according to your concern and your words, take Joshua. And know that he is a man in whom is ruach, meaning: you are the root of all the souls, and he exists in the aspect of ruach. And this is what it says <b>a man in whom is ruach</b> — meaning, the root of all the ruchot (spirits) of that generation. And HaShem commanded to lean his hand, to awaken in the ruach the essence of the soul that is in Moses, and this is what it says at the end <b>that all the congregation of the children of Israel may hear</b> — juxtaposed to the statement ״and you shall lay of your hod upon him,״ to say that through this he would also be included from the root of the souls, and through this ״they shall hear,״ meaning they will receive his words, ״all the congregation of the children of Israel״ — meaning, the disposition of the complete people, possessors of a soul pleasing from him, will also come about."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:39.944356756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}